# Collectors & legal

Priority order for new sources:

1. RSS / public feeds  
2. Official APIs when keys exist  
3. Customer-owned exports the brand/agency has rights to use  
4. Curated public pages only if ToS/robots allow  
5. Licensed social firehose partners (roadmap)

## Hard limits

- User-Agent: `RadArtBot/1.0`
- Rate-limit + timeouts; no infinite crawl
- No login walls, paywall bypass, or private social scrapes
- No unofficial Facebook / Instagram / TikTok scrapers
- No mock / seeded fake media for demos — empty states when signal is thin
- Collect only: title, URL, date, source, short text, public engagement when available

## Tunisia reality

MVP stack (RSS, Reddit, Google News, iTunes, optional YouTube/Trends) is strong for demos.
Serious cultural intelligence needs denser FB/IG/TikTok signal via **official APIs**, **customer-owned data**, or **licensed providers** — never compliance shortcuts.

## Implementation

- One collector module per source family; register in the ingestion pipeline.
- Fail soft: log/skip, never abort the whole `collect_all` run.
- Normalize to the shared media-item shape before ingest.
- Keep `/api/sources/coverage` honest about live vs needs_key vs planned vs forbidden.
